            "name": "Plotly Dash",
            "version": "4.4.1"
          },
          "instructions": "This is a Fast Dash app: a Python callback rendered as a web UI, with a live browser session a human may be watching.\n\nUnlike a plain Dash app, this app's tools are STATEFUL -- they drive the running app, and what you do IS reflected in the user's browser (within about 500ms, no reload):\n  - describe_app() -- start here: every input's id, type, default, allowed options and current value, plus the outputs a run produces.\n  - set_input(component_id, value) / set_inputs(inputs) -- set values; the browser's widgets update to match.\n  - invoke(inputs=None) -- set values and run the callback in one call; the output renders in the browser and the result is returned to you.\n  - set_form(specs) -- DynamicDash only: build the input form at runtime.\n\nValues are validated against the contract describe_app() advertises, so you cannot set something the UI itself could not produce."
        }
      }
